            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h1 id=\"environment-and-gpu-setup\">Environment and GPU setup</h1>\n<span class=\"paragraph\"><a href=\"https://molab.marimo.io/github/Quantum-Light-Matter-Cooperative-QLMC/pyrite/blob/main/docs/notebooks/00-setup.py\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\"><img alt=\"Open in Molab\" src=\"https://marimo.io/molab-shield.svg\" /></a></span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Verify your Python environment, choose a backend, and complete one tiny CPU simulation.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "vblA",
      "code_hash": "3e0266649ab37c52c206faa214f0860b",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h2 id=\"install-and-fetch-tables-once\">Install and fetch tables once</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Use Python <strong>3.13 or newer</strong>. Locally, create an environment and install:</span>\n<div class=\"language-bash codehilite\"><pre><span></span><code>uv<span class=\"w\"> </span>venv<span class=\"w\"> </span>--python<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"m\">3</span>.13\nuv<span class=\"w\"> </span>pip<span class=\"w\"> </span>install<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s1\">'pyrite-mc[apps]==0.22.4'</span>\nuv<span class=\"w\"> </span>run<span class=\"w\"> </span>pyrite<span class=\"w\"> </span>tables<span class=\"w\"> </span>fetch\nuv<span class=\"w\"> </span>run<span class=\"w\"> </span>pyrite<span class=\"w\"> </span>tables<span class=\"w\"> </span>verify\nuv<span class=\"w\"> </span>run<span class=\"w\"> </span>marimo<span class=\"w\"> </span>edit<span class=\"w\"> </span>docs/notebooks/00-setup.py\n</code></pre></div>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">The reference data download is about 100 MB. Fetch verifies archive SHA-256\nbefore installation; <code>tables verify</code> checks installed pins and payloads.\nThe setup cell calls <code>pyrite.fetch_tables()</code> to install missing pinned tables\nautomatically. Complete installations are reused without a network request.\nThe CLI commands above remain useful for manual verification or troubleshooting.\nSee the <a href=\"https://pyrite.readthedocs.io/en/latest/repo-design/cli/cli-reference-tables.html\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">tables reference</a>.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\"><strong>Molab:</strong> open the badge above; its inline dependency manifest installs the\nCPU environment. The first cell fetches missing tables automatically; you can\nrun <code>pyrite tables verify</code> in Molab's terminal. Start with CPU. If your Molab\nsession offers an NVIDIA RTX Pro 6000, select that GPU in Molab, then install\nthe NVIDIA extra into the\nsame environment:</span>\n<div class=\"language-bash codehilite\"><pre><span></span><code>uv<span class=\"w\"> </span>pip<span class=\"w\"> </span>install<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s1\">'pyrite-mc[nvidia]==0.22.4'</span>\nnvidia-smi\n</code></pre></div>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Use the same extra for a local NVIDIA GPU. A compatible NVIDIA driver is still\nrequired; the current extra supplies CUDA 13 CuPy/toolkit packages. GPU type,\navailability and account quotas depend on the host. This notebook does not\nrequire a GPU or allocate GPU transport by default.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
