          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h2 id=\"continue\">Continue</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">This tiny, fixed-seed run verifies that the selected backend can produce finite,\nnonzero spectral data with the installed tables. It is <strong>not a convergence or\nphysics-validation test</strong>. The histories are numerical samples, not a physical\nbeam charge. Check the <a href=\"https://pyrite.readthedocs.io/en/latest/validation/status-summary.html\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">validation status</a>\nfor scientific evidence and limitations.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Continue with <strong>01 \u2014 Your first X-ray spectrum</strong>. Keep the core sequence on CPU\nuntil workload size justifies a GPU. GPU outputs can differ across architectures;\ncompare physically meaningful quantities with justified tolerances, not exact\nrandom-history identity.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
